        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF144 added a new constraint parameter <code class=\"notranslate\">resizeMode</code> for use with <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/MediaDevices/getUserMedia\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">MediaDevices.getUserMedia()</code></a> and <code class=\"notranslate\">getDisplayMedia()</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This allows a developer to specify whether the video from the camera should be cropped and/or downscaled to match other constraints, which may be natively supported by the camera - essentially gives them what they ask for rather than what the camera is capable of delivering. It also allows them to specify that it doesn't want scaling.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This updates the relevant docs (First two commits are layout only).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The main changes are to:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Better cross-link <code class=\"notranslate\">MediaTrackConstraints</code> which is where the constraint is documented to make it clear that it is also used in these methods (not just some others).</li>\n<li>Provide an example explaining the downscaling.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3417378973\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41132\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41132/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41132\">#41132</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41153",
            "title": "Get user media constraints resizemode",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-17T23:30:35.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-16T05:59:32.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF144 added a new constraint parameter <code class=\"notranslate\">resizeMode</code> for use with <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/MediaDevices/getUserMedia\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">MediaDevices.getUserMedia()</code></a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This allows a developer to specify whether the video from the camera should be cropped and/or downscaled to match other constraints, which may be natively supported by the camera - essentially gives them what they ask for rather than what the camera is capable of delivering.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds a release note.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3417378973\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41132\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41132/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41132\">#41132</a></p>",
